> How do you say in Lojban "I buy it whatever it costs"?

How about:

  {vecnu ta mi seja'i da .oicu'i jdima}

or roughly, "I buy it, with requirement that something
(about which I am indifferent) is the price."

This raised another question for me; I though of using {ki'u}
(agentive motivation) instead of {seja'i}, but then it seems that
it would have referred to the motivation of the seller, not me,
the buyer.  If I had said {mi te vecnu ta ki'u...} instead of
{vecnu ta mi ki'u...}, would that have implied that I was
talking about the buyer's motivation?

